                    '2. Warning about Q09. The sick leave question is tricky because clause 2.4 is about sickness. It says to tell the line manager by 9:00 am and to give a medical note after 2 consecutive days of absence. It gives no number of paid sick days, and that is why the key marks Q09 as not answerable. A tool that quotes 2.4 accurately and says the handbook gives no number is behaving well. A tool that turns 2.4 into a number of days has invented one. Do not call an answer wrong only because it mentions 2.4. Judge whether a number appears and where it came from.',
                    '3. Case A, no file. Open a new chat with no file. Ask: How many working days of paid annual leave does a full-time staff member at Nile Valley Foods earn each year? Read the answer aloud and record it.',
                    '4. If the tool says it cannot know the policy of Nile Valley Foods, say: Good. That is the behaviour we want. Now what if it had not said so? Then go on. If it gives a number, ask the class how sure it sounds and whether it could know the rules of a fictional company. The key answer comes in the next step.',
                    '5. Case B, with the file. Open a new chat. Attach staff_handbook_excerpt.txt, ask the same question, and add: Quote the exact words you used. The key answer is 21 working days, clause 2.1. Find the quoted words in the file together and record whether the quote is exact.',
